// expect: 44
// mn-fn-tuple-param.mn — pattern params on NAMED fns (SYNTAX.md §Pattern
// syntax: patterns appear in let, match, function parameters, and lambda
// parameters). The lambda half was proven by mn-tuple-lambda; this pins the
// named-fn half through the same desugar (fresh param + prepend-let,
// bind_param_destructures) for all three shapes the lambda path runs:
// tuple f=7, record g=30, exact-length list h=7 → 44.
// A pattern in parameter position is an arm on the argument, so an
// exact-length list there leaves every other length untaken — inexhaustive,
// and every error refuses. The refusable destructure is written where
// SYNTAX puts it: a `let` whose refusal the foot of the chain answers.
fn f((a, b)) = a + b
fn g({x, y}) = x * y
fn h(xs) = {
  let [p, q] = xs
  p - q
} ~> otherwise(0)
fn main() = f((3, 4)) + g({x: 5, y: 6}) + h([10, 3])
